{
  "company_name": "ChipFlow Supply",
  "industry": "Semiconductor",
  "use_case": "Semiconductor demand forecasting and order backlog management",
  "space_title": "ChipFlow - Demand Forecasting 📈",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Semiconductor\n\n**Use case:** Semiconductor Demand Forecasting & Backlog Management\n\nChipFlow Supply — demand sensing and order-book analytics across 20 product SKUs sold through OEM Tier 1, OEM Tier 2, Distributor, Contract Manufacturer, and Direct Enterprise channels. Product end-markets span automotive (MCU-32 Automotive, PMIC Automotive), industrial controllers, consumer SoCs, and connectivity ICs. Sales Ops and Demand Planning use this space to monitor forecast accuracy and backlog aging; the Supply Chain VP and CFO use it to flag book-to-bill inflection points, segment-level demand softness, and SKUs at risk of allocation or write-down given semiconductor cycle volatility.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Forecast accuracy % — 1-MAPE on units forecast; world-class semis target 70%+, with leading-edge SKUs often 50-60%\n- Backlogged order count — orders past quoted lead time; leading indicator of capacity or yield issues\n- Book-to-bill ratio — bookings vs shipments; >1.0 indicates growing demand, <1.0 contraction\n- Lead time (days) — quoted vs achieved; semi industry median 12–26 weeks during shortage cycles\n- Weeks of supply — committed vs available inventory; healthy 8–16 weeks\n- Total order revenue (USD) — top-line demand signal\n- Forecast bias — chronic over/under bias by SKU category\n- Customer segment concentration — share of revenue at-risk by segment\n\n**Data sources**\n- `customer_orders` — daily customer orders with quantity, price, lead time, fulfillment status\n- `demand_forecasts` — weekly forecasted vs actual demand with model accuracy and bias\n- `inventory_positions` — monthly on-hand, committed, and available units with weeks of supply",
  "schema_basename": "semiconductor_demand_forecast",
