  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Demand Forecasting and order-book management for a semiconductor distributor serving 20 SKUs across Automotive, Industrial, Consumer, and Data Center segments. Stakeholders include Demand Planning (forecast accuracy, bias), Sales Ops (backlog aging, lead time), and the Supply Chain VP (book-to-bill, weeks of supply, allocation risk). Semi cycles swing book-to-bill from 0.7 (downturn) to 1.3 (shortage), and lead-time inflation is the earliest predictor of cycle inflection.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Forecast accuracy = avg_forecast_accuracy_pct (1-MAPE); semi target 70%+, leading-edge SKUs often 50–60%\n- Forecast bias = forecast_bias label (Over / Under / Neutral)\n- Backlog = fulfillment_status = 'Backlogged' (orders past quoted lead time)\n- Lead time = lead_time_days; healthy 56–84 days, shortage cycles 168–365 days\n- Weeks of supply = weeks_of_supply; healthy 8–16, >20 flags excess, <4 flags stockout risk\n- Order revenue = order_revenue_usd; top-line demand\n- Available to ship = available_units in inventory_positions\n- Customer segments: OEM Tier 1, OEM Tier 2, Distributor, Contract Manufacturer, Direct Enterprise\n- Regions: Asia Pacific, North America, Europe, Greater China, Rest of World\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - customer_order_metrics (source: customer_orders) — dims: order_date, product_category, customer_segment, fulfillment_status, region; measures: total_orders, total_order_revenue_usd, total_units_ordered, avg_lead_time_days, backlogged_order_count, total_unit_price, unique_sku_count, max_order_quantity.\n  - forecast_accuracy_metrics (source: demand_forecasts) — dims: forecast_date, product_category, forecast_bias, model_type; measures: avg_forecast_accuracy_pct, total_forecasted_units, total_actual_units, total_forecast_records, unique_sku_count, max_forecasted_units.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. sku_id, sku_name, on_hand_units, committed_units, available_units, weeks_of_supply, inventory_health).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Which 10 SKUs have the highest backlogged order count, and what is our exposed revenue?",
    "Show monthly total order revenue by customer segment for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which product categories have the worst forecast accuracy this quarter — where do we need model retraining?",
    "Rank the 5 customer regions by average lead time — where is lead-time inflation worst?",
    "How has total units ordered trended monthly by product category — is book-to-bill turning?",
    "Which SKUs have less than 4 weeks of supply this month and are at stockout risk?",
    "What is the total forecasted vs actual units in the trailing 6 months, and which categories are chronically Over or Under?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique skus?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(unique_sku_count) AS unique_sku_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.customer_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest order quantity changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(max_order_quantity) AS max_order_quantity",
        "FROM {fqn}.customer_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest forecasted units?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_date, MEASURE(max_forecasted_units) AS max_forecasted_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.forecast_accuracy_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total number of units ordered break down by product sku identifier for 'Shipped' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT sku_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(order_quantity) AS total_order_quantity",
        "FROM {fqn}.customer_orders",
        "WHERE fulfillment_status = 'Shipped' GROUP BY sku_id ORDER BY total_order_quantity DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total predicted demand in units over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_date, SUM(forecasted_units) AS total_forecasted_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY forecast_date ORDER BY forecast_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct unique inventory position record identifier are there per product category grouping?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT product_category, COUNT(DISTINCT position_id) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_positions",
        "GROUP BY product_category ORDER BY distinct_count DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total unit price usd changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(total_unit_price) AS total_unit_price",
        "FROM {fqn}.customer_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
